This is a flat spring of stainless steel, so it falls under heading 7320 (springs and leaves for springs, of iron or steel). The flat spring is not a leaf spring, helical spring, or coil spring, so it goes in the "other" subheading. Within 7320.90, the "other" line is 7320.90.50 (other, including stainless?). The 7320.90 subheadings are 7320.90.10 (Other: of stainless?) — more precisely, I recall 7320.90.10 as "Flat springs" in older schedules, but the current schedule is 7320.90.5010 (Other, "Other") and 7320.90.5030 (Other). I'm not fully certain of the statistical suffix, so I use the general "other" line.

The classification is probably CBP ruling-based, 7320.90.5010 (Other: Other: Other, covering stainless?). I'll go with 7320.90.5010.

{"hts_code": "7320.90.5010", "reason": "A stainless steel flat spring clip that functions through spring compression is classified as an iron or steel spring under heading 7320, in the 'other' subheading 7320.90."}
